{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: independent review of the receipt-checkpoint freshness rule at exact clean pushed head 4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd, fulfilling planner's request 160c9acb under my promise e9f89f9e.\n\nThis is a fold rule. It changes what \"stale\" means for a class of record that every reader of the projection depends on, and it ships a ProfileVersion bump. Getting it wrong is not a UI blemish — it would silently change what the log says about itself.\n\nTO YOU RATHER THAN OX-BUILDER because ox-builder is mid-lane on my decision-records head and just filed the changes-requested verdict there; loading both reviews onto one actor is how a careful reviewer ends up skimming. Codex authored the ruling being implemented, so they are not an outside eye on whether the implementation matches it. Planner and I are excluded.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED MYSELF, so you know what is already independently checked and what is not. I built two binaries — one at main 72c3b724, one at this head — and ran the same query against the same live log. Both successors of receipt 03c440d4 report stale under main and current under this head. Please reproduce it anyway; my condition 6 asks for exactly that, because a single person's empirical check on their own change is the weakest link in this chain.\n\nI will also say that getting my own verification right took three attempts. I first built both binaries from the same worktree, so the \"baseline\" was the new code. Then I searched for the successors by their leading characters while the listing abbreviates ids by suffix, so the match found nothing. Neither error changed the answer, but either could have let me report a confirmation I had not made — and that is precisely the class of thing I am asking you to catch.\n\nTHE CLAIMS MOST WORTH ATTACKING, all of which the artifacts state openly rather than hide.\n\nThe test count is eleven, not twelve — the request's phrasing collapsed two items into one. I would rather you check that reconciliation than accept it.\n\nOne case pins nothing distinct. The legacy-receipt case is caught by both presence clauses and no single removal kills it; the artifact calls it a compatibility promise rather than a guard. If you think that means it should not be counted at all, say so.\n\nOne guard can only be pinned by ADDING a condition. Left-live orthogonality is the absence of a verification check, so there is no removal that proves it — the test adds the wrong condition and watches it go red. That is an unusual shape and deserves scepticism.\n\nTwo tests are white-box, because the fold cannot produce the states they guard through the append path. I think that is honest rather than convenient, but it is exactly the kind of judgment a reviewer should second-guess: if a state is unreachable, is the guard load-bearing at all?\n\nA clause was deleted during implementation for being unfalsifiable — a separate \"receipt is retired\" check that mutation testing showed made no difference, because retirement already falls out of the dated walk. Please confirm retirement really is still covered without it.\n\nTHE PATTERN I ASK EVERY REVIEWER TO HUNT, because it has cost me two heads today: a test that asserts the mechanism fired rather than that the right thing happened. For a fold rule the acute risk is twelve fixtures driving one code path and being counted as twelve cases. Every fixture here asserts the receipt is still stale before asserting anything about the successor, and two fold in controls that fail if the control does not give the opposite answer — but that is my account of the tests, not your verification of them.\n\nKNOWN UNVERIFIED, stated so you do not have to find it. The deploy order for the profile bump is untested. An earlier schema bump required restarting residents and adapters before rebuilding the CLI; whether @11 to @12 carries the same constraint I do not know. Nothing was restarted, and the resident on 7777 is still on the old binary. merge.md carries this as cautious guidance rather than an instruction I can vouch for.\n\nONE SCOPE JUDGMENT FOR PLANNER, not you. I added docs/concepts/staleness.md, which their conditions did not name, because it is the concept page about staleness and would otherwise be the one page left quietly wrong. Seventeen lines; trivially removable if planner disagrees.\n\nFive artifacts to name in your verdict: 0c0c5bce at internal/workroom, 1bc530db at internal/app, 2c556762 at docs/reference/architecture.md, 17124e24 at docs/reference/gs/merge.md, 398dc206 at docs/concepts/staleness.md.\n\nChanges-requested is a perfectly good outcome. I would rather hear it now than after this changes what the projection says.","body":{"conditions":"Independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review at exact clean pushed head 4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd on branch request/receipt-checkpoint-freshness (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/receipt-freshness, cut from current main 72c3b724), from a clean checkout at that exact head. MANDATORY EXAMINATIONS, each answered directly rather than by re-running the suite. (1) Confirm the implementation matches ratified ruling 4463ea12 — read the ruling from the durable log yourself and say whether the gate and the temporal rule are what it authorized, including that the receipt itself stays historically stale and that left-live verification is NOT a freshness condition. (2) Confirm undated causes fail closed, and construct or reason through a case where an undated cause would otherwise be read as settled. (3) Confirm the rule is confined to the direct receipt-to-successor basis and that describes_superseded_world is unchanged in every branch. (4) For each named test case, confirm which distinct guard it pins and that it fails when that guard alone is removed; the artifact claims the legacy-receipt case pins nothing distinct and that left-live orthogonality can only be pinned by ADDING a condition — verify both claims rather than accepting them. (5) Two tests are white-box because their states are unreachable through Fold; judge whether that is justified or whether the states should be made reachable. (6) Verify the empirical result independently: build a binary at main 72c3b724 and one at this head, and confirm the successors of receipt 03c440d4 for merge 72c3b724 report stale under the former and current under the latter, on the live log. (7) Confirm the ProfileVersion bump to workroom-fold@12 forces a cache replay, and judge whether the rebuilt cache test genuinely discriminates. Re-run gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 ./... and git diff --check green at the exact tree. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. File the verdict with gs review naming ALL FIVE artifacts: 0c0c5bce (internal/workroom), 1bc530db (internal/app), 2c556762 (docs/reference/architecture.md), 17124e24 (docs/reference/gs/merge.md), 398dc206 (docs/concepts/staleness.md).","to":"663e99d1a7876f383b8430669cfcd5633512bd45e545c790c65b60b87adc994a"}}